s Is Not an Exit: The Fictional World of Bret Easton Ellis, exploring the controversial American author of American Psycho and Less Than Zero, known for his sharp satire on materialism, media, and youth culture in the 80s and 90s, often featuring vapid characters and dark themes. The show, featuring Ellis, Will Self, and Rachel Weisz, delved into his themes of image, consumption, and the superficiality of beauty and fame, as seen in novels like Glamorama, which critiques image-obsessed worlds where \\\"image is truth\\\".\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event.\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2026-01-09T16:45:00+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-03-21T13:30:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2026-01-09T16:45:00+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-03-21T14:00:00+00:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-03-21T15:30:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"previews\":[],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null}],\"title\":\"Sat 21 Mar\",\"image\":null,\"key\":null,\"action\":null,\"subtitle\":null,\"suggestion_type\":null,\"suggestion_name\":null,\"section_type\":\"events_vertical\",\"load_more\":null,\"section_hash\":null},{\"events\":[{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[],\"total_artists\":0,\"total_free_texts\":2},\"offers_extras\":false,\"donation\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Dash The Henge Store\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"film\",\"value\":\"culture:film\",\"title\":\"Film\"}],\"faqs\":[],\"max_tickets\":6,\"properties\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"10156\",\"name\":\"Live At St Giles\",\"address\":\"Camberwell Church Street, Southwark, London, SE5 8RB, United Kingdom\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.47364,\"lng\":-0.08961},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0