ix\":1770768000,\"max_tickets\":4,\"marketeers\":[],\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"seating\":null,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Suren Seneviratne is an eclectic music producer and purveyor of strange sounds. Since 2011 he has formed extensively across Europe, presenting a number of electronic works that have disobeyed genre classification.\\n\\nHis latest project 𝙼𝙸𝚂𝚂𝙸𝙽𝙶 𝙼𝚄𝚂𝙸𝙲 is part software archeology and part improvised musical performance. It shines a spotlight on the innovative DSP software developed for Mac computers during the ‘90s to ‘00s. Original iBook G4 and PowerBook G4 laptops are used in performance to create live, electronic music using software taken from the blog, showcasing the audio/visual aesthetic of the millennium.\\n\\nKate Carr is a composer and sound artist whose work centres on field recording, listening practices, and the politics of sound. Her performances weave together environmental recordings, subtle electronics, and archival material, creating immersive sound worlds that reward close attention. Carr’s work sits at the intersection of sound art, experimental music, and ecological inquiry, and is known for its quiet intensity and emotional depth.\\n\\nMisery Bacon is the solo experimental sound and noise project of Norwegian-based artist, illustrator, and musician Luke Drozd. Associated with Bloxham Tapes, the project explores collage, soundscapes, and harsh noise, often moving between abrasion and atmosphere.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by MULTI STORY.\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"impression_id\":\"7edfaa6f16d85d00:49\",\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/c219e4925177?dice_id=c219e4925177\",\