e,\"date_unix\":1772047800,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"impression_id\":\"4699078e3c3acde4:53\",\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":2781},\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"streaming_options\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/b8c96fe1-8615-4df6-9b7f-f0c3c2c74a82.jpg?rect=542%2C0%2C3672%2C3672\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/b8c96fe1-8615-4df6-9b7f-f0c3c2c74a82.jpg?rect=0%2C409%2C4756%2C2854\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/b8c96fe1-8615-4df6-9b7f-f0c3c2c74a82.jpg?rect=1368%2C0%2C2020%2C3672\"},\"id\":\"68a731377840140001445fb2\",\"name\":\"Black Honey\",\"seating\":null,\"secondary_status\":\"waiting-list\",\"new\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Black Honey return with Soak, their most raw and emotionally resonant album yet. Led by the ever-electric Izzy B. Phillips, the Brighton quartet (Chris Ostler, Tommy Taylor, Alex Woodward) take a bold leap into vulnerability and sonic ambition.\\n\\nWoozily dramatic and crammed with the kind of killer melodies we’ve come to expect from a Black Honey record, Soak is unapologetically led from the gut, and even stronger for its emotional vulnerabilities. Having channelled Quentin Tarantino and Wes Anderson on previous albums, Phillips cites Stanley Kubrick as a key inspiration for the visual universe of Soak, specifically the retro-futurism of A Clockwork Orange, The Shining and 2001: A Space Odyssey.\\n\\nFour albums in, Black Honey’s ambition and unstudied authenticity remain as bold and captivating as ever.\\n\\nIf you have any queries or would like more information about access at Village Underground, please see our FAQs here: https://bit.ly/3EhSLgF, or contact access@villageunderground.co.uk.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"16+ event. (16-17 with a responsible adult 18+,1:1) \",\"subtitle\":null,\