l,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"corsica-studios-jqna\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.corsicastudios.com/information/accessibility\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"927\",\"name\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2023-11-17/84092575-7b18-48f1-a81d-3e429d6f7b2b.jpg\"},\"perm_name\":\"baba-yagas-hut-l8ob\",\"profile_active\":true},\"announcement_date_unix\":1760518800,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/E8c8821e07c4?dice_id=E8c8821e07c4\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Mf15064b3a0f?dice_id=Mf15064b3a0f\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/h6930523d59c?dice_id=h6930523d59c\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Q746c2f4a3fa?dice_id=Q746c2f4a3fa\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/B5adfe35b574?dice_id=B5adfe35b574\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/w633311ebf2d?dice_id=w633311ebf2d\"},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"perm_name\":\"yog2xx-teeth-of-the-sea-microcorps-11th-mar-corsica-studios-london-tickets\",\"unicorn\":true,\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":222,\"name\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.babayagashut.com/privacy-policy\",\"fb_pixel_id\":\"1263983106946503\",\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"date_unix\":1773257400,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"impression_id\":\"49dcf1c1636e57c2:45\",\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":1800,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"streaming_options\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-14/32c1ac5e-48dc-4a37-9c80-1b05a55d3f63.jpg?rect=199%2C0%2C883%2C883\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-14/32c1ac5e-48dc-4a37-9c80-1b05a55d3f63.jpg?rect=0%2C58%2C1280%2C768\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-14/32c1ac5e-48dc-4a37-9c80-1b05a55d3f63.jpg?rect=397%2C0%2C486%2C883\"},\"id\":\"68e3dccce3870c0001997f42\",\"name\":\"Teeth of the Sea + MICROCORPS\",\"seating\":null,\"secondary_status\":null,\"new\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut Presents:\\n\\nTeeth of the Sea + MICROCORPS\\n\\nCorsica Studios - March 11th\\n\\nBlasting their way through all or any genre distinctions in a storied journey across the chaos and nonsense of sixteen years, London’s Teeth Of The Sea remain true to their original mission - to set sparks flying at the meeting point between raw noise and rich atmosphere. Thundering beat-driven abandon, chaotic psychedelia, heavy melancholia and indelible melody have all coalesced and converged on their five albums for Rocket Recording\\n\\nFrom the basements of East London, Teeth Of The Sea have forged forward intrepidly over twelve years, four albums and two EPs to become heralded as the UK’s most adventurous and unclassifiable outfit in the realm of the psychedelic. As inspired by virulent garage-driven noise as austere avant-garde experimentation and driven by soundtrack atmospherics, jazz exploration and electronic dissonance alike, they’ve outgrown their original influences (Butthole Surfers, Eno, Goblin, Aphex Twin, Throbbing Gristle) to forge a sound both richly celestial and acidically synapse-scorching.\\n\\nIt’s a journey that’s taken them to European festivals like Roadburn, Milhoes De Festa, Eindhoven Psych Lab and Incubate, seen them perform specially curated live soundtrack work in Romania, Cork and CERN, and led them to devastate UK events like Supersonic, Supernormal, Latitude, Bestival and Green Man – all the while forging forward heedlessly into chaos and fresh discovery anew. With each new album set to further terrify and transfix in ways never heard before, Teeth Of The Sea continue to blaze forth with enlightenment and irreverence to the fore. Who knows where they’ll arrive, but be prepared to brace yourself and bear witness\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-10-15T10:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T18:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-10-15T10:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T22:30:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Teeth Of The Sea - Field Punishment\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/0pX8l3syErEZKaj1LsbnId\",\"artist\":\"Teeth Of The Sea\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/c6b8b368726f23cdb9eaa97fdbbaf7c865cd652f?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"Field Punishment\"},{\"type\":\"apple_music\",\"title\":\"Teeth of the Sea - Field Punishment\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/field-punishment/1031236153?i=1031236162&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"Teeth of the Sea\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview20/v4/02/cb/b3/02cbb3fc-0344-18d0-ea92-4349dd3e2a81/mzaf_7766567421170186759.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"Field Punishment\"}],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null},{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"The Antlers\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-i-scdn-co.imgix.net/image/ab6761610000e5ebcd1e2ce5e1c01ab4a3cb0bf9\"},\"artist_id\":\"10746\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":true},{\"name\":\"Julie Odell\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2022-05-12/b95d1f50-63f3-4d8c-8fd8-ddfa01a46202.jpg?rect=1%2C0%2C638%2C638\"},\"artist_id\":\"50364\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":2,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"offers_extras\":false,\"donation\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Parallel Lines + Live Nation. \",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"faqs\":[{\"id\":39692,\"title\":\"What are the age restrictions for this event?\",\"body\":\"This is a 16+ event. All attendees 16-17s must be accompanied by a responsible adult who is 18 or older (1:1 ratio). To verify age, ID may be requested. We advise all customers to bring valid ID. For further information, see Age and ID in FAQs. Right of admission reserved.\",\"order\":0}],\"max_tickets\":6,\"properties\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"1955\",\"name\":\"EartH\",\"address\":\"11 Stoke Newington Rd, London N16 8BH, UK\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5509892,\"lng\":-0.07532500000002074},\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2023-02-02/92037b31-0756-4c73-9f1b-11e5c4753296.jpg?rect=683%2C0%2C1365%2C1365\"},\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"earth-76a7\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://bit.ly/44dzl75\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":\"EartH Theatre\",\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"11564\",\"name\":\"EartH\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"earth-yxox\",\"profile_active\":false},\"announcement_date_unix\":1756890000,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/n285a4c6caf1?dice_id=n285a4c6caf1\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/t88c11e58658?dice_id=t88c11e58658\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r48a6f0ff0c6?dice_id=r48a6f0ff0c6\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/W65249a3d451?dice_id=W65249a3d451\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Qce171573f82?dice_id=Qce171573f82\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/v8dd64e4f8ad?dice_id=v8dd64e4f8ad\"},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"perm_name\":\"bb57om-the-antlers-11th-mar-earth-london-tickets\",\"unicorn\":false,\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":863,\"name\":\"EartH\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://earthackney.co.uk/privacy-policy/\",\"fb_pixel_id\":\"498772217287544\",\"ga_tracking_id\":\"G-6QJEY8LKG2\",\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":\"781332317\",\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":\"nxkPCNyPg5caEN3eyPQC\",\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"date_unix\":1773257400,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"impression_id\":\"49dcf1c1636e57c2:46\",\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":3271},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"streaming_options\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-09-02/0412e1ad-b5b8-494a-905c-6e0d6ce8a125.jpg?rect=200%2C0%2C1200%2C1200\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-09-02/0412e1ad-b5b8-494a-905c-6e0d6ce8a125.jpg?rect=0%2C120%2C1600%2C960\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-09-02/0412e1ad-b5b8-494a-905c-6e0d6ce8a125.jpg?rect=470%2C0%2C660%2C1200\"},\"id\":\"68a72da97840140001168f8d\",\"name\":\"The Antlers\",\"seating\":null,\"secondary_status\":null,\"new\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"This event will take place in EartH Theatre.\\n\\nThe follow-up to 2021’s rustic, folk-tinged Green to Gold, Blight asks many questions without offering easy answers. Over the course of nine new songs, the Antlers’ founder and primary. songwriter Silberman reckons with our passively destructive tendencies – absentminded pollution, unwitting wastefulness, and the inadvertent devastation of the natural world. But despite its heavy themes, Blight is far from a punishing listen. With its adventurous arrangements and persistent momentum, it plays more like an iridescent odyssey.\\n\\nThe album was recorded over the course of a few years, with the lion’s share tracked and produced in Silberman’s home studio in upstate New York, a compact outbuilding perched at the edge of a neighbor’s sprawling hayfield. “So much of the record was conceived while walking these massive fields,” he says. “I felt like I was wandering around an abandoned planet.” And in a sense, Blight does feel like science fiction, sounding as if it were delivered from the near future. The album is a work of meticulous world-building, teeming with ear candy and surprising stylistic shifts. While many songs begin with sparse elements— a fingerpicked guitar, hypnotic organ stabs, or a nimble piano melody — they rarely remain tethered to their foundations. They often reimagine themselves partway through, shifting mid-track from gentle ballad to throbbing electronica, only to land somewhere entirely different by the end.\\n\\nSilberman has been confronting weighty matters ever since The Antlers’ 2009 breakthrough Hospice, an unrelentingly heavy concept album about a child cancer patient and her caregiver that addressed psychological abuse and post-traumatic stress with explicit detail and unflinching vulnerability, resonating equally with those grieving loved ones and rocky relationships. The album’s ambitious sonics— an unlikely amalgam of intimate folk confessionals, haunted soundscapes, and sky-scraping post-rock— belied its modest origins: Hospice was mostly recorded alone in Silberman’s Brooklyn bedroom, with an economy of equipment and hardly any expectant audience. The surprise popularity of Hospice placed the Antlers on a rapid ascent, touring globally, playing major festivals, and supporting such luminaries as The National and Explosions in the Sky.\\n\\nThe music that followed grew The Antlers’ sizable following while resisting the impulse to\\n\\nrehash their initial success. The electronic pop of 2011’s Burst Apart, the aquatic psychedelia of\\n\\n2012’s Undersea EP, and the brass-laden soul of 2014’s Familiars all embraced the band&#39;s\\n\\ningenuity while simultaneously subverting expectations, expanding the band’s emotional\\n\\npalette beyond the morose rage and desperation that characterized Hospice to reveal a playful\\n\\nexpansiveness. The Antlers further pushed the boundaries as a live entity, trading the lush\\n\\norchestration of their ambitious recordings for wall-of-sound maximalism and thunderous\\n\\ndynamics.\\n\\nSadly, Silberman was forced to scale back after an unexpected hearing incident left him\\n\\ntemporarily deaf in one ear and hypersensitive to sound. Putting The Antlers on pause, he\\n\\nmade 2017’s Impermanence, a meditative and minimal solo album, pairing his then-fragile\\n\\nvoice with gentle guitar and an abundance of silence. After regaining his hearing and recovering\\n\\nfrom vocal cord surgery, Silberman and longtime drummer Michael Lerner revived The Antlers\\n\\nfor 2021’s Green to Gold, a collection of songs notably devoid of the darkness that\\n\\ncharacterized the band’s previous work.\\n\\nFollowing Green to Gold, Silberman honed his collaborative chops, including co-producing Wild\\n\\nPink’s critically-acclaimed breakout ILYSM. Shortly thereafter, he released the debut album\\n\\nfrom Cowboy Sadness, his instrumental band with David Moore (Bing &amp; Ruth) and Nicholas\\n\\nPrincipe (Port St. Willow).\\n\\nDuring these intervening years between Antlers albums, Silberman and Lerner kept busy as\\n\\nwell, releasing a series of free-standing singles unified by The Antlers’ gift for acid-dipped\\n\\ntimbres, shape-shifting production, and impressionistic imagery.\\n\\n“These singles were metaphysical songs about connection with nature, which in turn put me in\\n\\ntouch with all the ways that nature is under threat,” he says. “The smell of wildfire smoke on a\\n\\nsunny afternoon, the sound of chainsaws on a hike through the woods — these contradictions\\n\\nbecame impossible to ignore.”\\n\\nWhereas The Antlers have previously dealt in extended metaphors, Blight now takes a more\\n\\ndirect approach. In “Calamity,” for instance, Silberman asks point-blank: “Who will look after\\n\\nwhat we leave behind?” The final and perhaps fundamental question posed by Blight appears in\\n\\nthe penultimate track, the tragically relevant futuristic hymnal “A Great Flood”, in which he\\n\\nwonders: “Will we be forgiven should there come a great flood to drown out our decisions?”\\n\\nThis question hangs in the air unanswered. Blight invites listeners to consider it for themselves,\\n\\nas if the survival of the natural world is in their hands, slowly slipping through their fingertips.\\n\\nFor more information on access at EartH, please see our FAQs here: https://bit.ly/44dzl75 or contact us at access@earthackney.co.uk\\n\\nEartH is a social enterprise committed to supporting new musicians, with music studios in the venue that are completely free for young artists in Hackney to use. Find out more here (https://earthackney.co.uk/about/studio-36/).\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"16+ event. (16-17 with a responsible adult 18+,1:1) \",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-09-03T10:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T21:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-09-05T10:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T23:00:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Kettering\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/453spNn4mGdYErYt3rGhSX\",\"artist\":\"\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/5597ae435008d3d0104598a1314053066429feba?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"Kettering\"},{\"type\":\"apple_music\",\"title\":\"The Antlers - I Don't Want Love\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/album/i-dont-want-love/671824827?i=671824830&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"The Antlers\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/apple-assets-us-std-000001/AudioPreview71/v4/01/cd/70/01cd70d9-07c4-fc33-9c5f-389203c3e461/mzaf_4775249687411660732.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"I Don't Want Love\"}],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null},{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Micah P. Hinson\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"4973\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Alessandro Asso Stefana\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"74063\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":2,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"offers_extras\":false,\"donation\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Eat Your Own Ears.\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"faqs\":[],\"max_tickets\":6,\"properties\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"21\",\"name\":\"Oslo Hackney\",\"address\":\"1a Amhurst Road, Hackney, London, E8 1LL, United Kingdom\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.54716,\"lng\":-0.05558},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"oslo-hackney-je6z\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.oslohackney.com/accessibility/\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"10\",\"name\":\"Eat Your Own Ears\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"eat-your-own-ears-z82z\",\"profile_active\":true},\"announcement_date_unix\":1748944800,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Pa42d63436fa?dice_id=Pa42d63436fa\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r49c66f8588d?dice_id=r49c66f8588d\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/y3a9f7cda426?dice_id=y3a9f7cda426\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/D5e6f9ec1dcb?dice_id=D5e6f9ec1dcb\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/G23b049c0105?dice_id=G23b049c0105\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Pee7995562f5?dice_id=Pee7995562f5\"},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"perm_name\":\"nvbdb3-micah-p-hinson-11th-mar-oslo-hackney-london-tickets\",\"unicorn\":false,\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_disabled\"},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":1337,\"name\":\"Eat Your Own Ears\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.eatyourownears.com/privacy-cookies-policy/\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"date_unix\":1773257400,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"impression_id\":\"49dcf1c1636e57c2:47\",\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":2285,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"streaming_options\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-06-02/7a18d714-6d4f-4977-89c8-82d657dbfa0b.jpg?rect=0%2C667%2C1333%2C1333\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-06-02/7a18d714-6d4f-4977-89c8-82d657dbfa0b.jpg?rect=0%2C600%2C1333%2C800\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-06-02/7a18d714-6d4f-4977-89c8-82d657dbfa0b.jpg?rect=117%2C0%2C1100%2C2000\"},\"id\":\"683d7ccce4dea3000145bd40\",\"name\":\"Micah P. Hinson\",\"seating\":null,\"secondary_status\":\"rescheduled\",\"new\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Eat Your Own Ears presents Micah P. Hinson at Oslo.\\n\\nIn early 2020, Micah P. Hinson almost walked away from his music career. The esoteric Americana / folk singer-songwriter – who divides his time between Texas and Spain – had released ten critically acclaimed albums and built up a loyal fanbase (particularly in Europe), yet he felt trapped and deeply depressed.\\n\\nBorn in Memphis but raised in Texas, Hinson didn’t initially understand his uniqueness. For one thing, he is of Chickasaw descent, a Native American tribe known for being particularly fierce warriors. For another, his family belonged to The Church of Christ, which is, as he explains it, “one of the newest and the strictest and the most bizarre sects of Christianity.”\\n\\nWhile Hinson has earned much acclaim by creating songs about his past – and no doubt I Lie to You will continue this tradition – it will be fascinating to see what he creates now that he can move on, free from all the things that had been weighing him down for years.\\n\\nAlready, he feels revitalized in every way: “It’s not only my songwriting that changed, but my family life, my views on religion, and my views on politics,” he says. “It's really strange that I decided to make these changes in my life, and then so many amazing, beautiful things came to me. I'll be forever grateful for whatever happened to bring me to this new place.”\\n\\nSupport from Alessandro \\\"Asso\\\" Stefana.\\n\\nAge restriction 16+ (under 18s accompanied by an adult)\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is a 16+ event (under 18’s accompanied). \",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-06-03T11:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T18:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-06-03T11:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00+00:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-03-11T23:30:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"previews\":[],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null},{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"The Destruction of The Cult of The Sun\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-02-20/a8aaf926-b487-4082-85b5-8accc7246ace.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C640%2C640\"},\"artist_id\":\"106118\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"offers_extras\":false,\"donation\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Kilimanjaro.\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"faqs\":[],\"max_tickets\":6,\"properties\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"8761\",\"name\":\"T