/1633803383?i=1633803384&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"Pentire\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview122/v4/17/89/e2/1789e2b5-6a42-a202-f5a4-2174d4e60991/mzaf_13427362075454376549.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"Best Friend's House\"}],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null},{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"EDEN\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2021-10-27/47beabcb-d40f-446e-a67e-d112924d161a.jpg?rect=0%2C14%2C613%2C613\"},\"artist_id\":\"2249\",\"about\":{\"description\":\"After shifting from the more straightforward dance music of his early days as the Eden Project, Jonathan Ng forged a new path as Eden. His 2020 outing, No Future, combined soulful R&B-inspired vocals with textured electronic pop, rock and dreamy ambience. This latest iteration plays to the Irish songwriter’s strengths, which lie in his vulnerability. Themes of loss, heartbreak and ephemerality are threaded throughout his electronic indie offerings, with glitchy, anxious sonics also a trademark.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":1},\"offers_extras\":false,\"donation\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Eat Your Own Ears.\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"faqs\":[{\"id\":23935,\"title\":\"What's the bag policy?\",\"body\":\"Security – Bag Policy\\n\\nLarge bags – including rucksacks are not allowed.\\n\\nThere are no facilities to leave large bags or luggage.\\n\\nIf you really have to bring a bag – and it’s preferable you don’t – please make sure it’s small.\\n\\nOnly one small bag per person is permitted and it must not be bigger than A4 size.\\n\\nHeight: 28.7cm\\n\\nWidth: 21cm\\n\\nDepth 15cm\",\"order\":0}],\"max_tickets\":6,\"properties\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"934\",\"name\":\"O2 Forum Kentish Town\",\"address\":\"9-17 Highgate Rd, London NW5 1JY\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5521427,\"lng\":-0.142224499999998},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"o2-forum-kentish-town-8er7\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://academymusicgroup.com/o2forumkentishtown/access\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-03-12T19:00:00+00:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"10\",\"name\":\"Eat Your Own Ears\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"eat-your-own-ears-z82z\",\"profile_active\":true},\"announcement_date_unix\":1755612000,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/d6ce459ad30a?dice_id=d6ce459ad30a\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/tfe9db9fdfde?dice_id=tfe9db9fdfde\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/kc75cf93d121?dice_id=kc75cf93d121\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Mc871dd5d783?dice_id=Mc871dd5d783\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/bd8a0a9b9794?dice_id=bd8a0a9b9794\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/t96603a48cd0?dice_id=t96603a48cd0\"},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"perm_name\":\"92p5gn-eden-12th-mar-o2-forum-kentish-town-london-tickets\",\"unicorn\":false,\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_disabled\"},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":1337,\"name\":\"Eat Your Own Ears\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.eatyourownears.com/privacy-cookies-policy/\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"date_unix\":1773342000,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"impression_id\":\"49dcf1c1636e57c2:71\",\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":3385},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"streaming_options\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-18/a81dcb43-0ecd-48e4-94c1-1221e1da6f2a.jpg?rect=912%2C0%2C3648%2C3648\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-18/a81dcb43-0ecd-48e4-94c1-1221e1da6f2a.jpg?rect=0%2C183%2C5472%2C3283\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-18/a81dcb43-0ecd-48e4-94c1-1221e1da6f2a.jpg?rect=1733%2C0%2C2006%2C3648\"},\"id\":\"68a35704a06e450001d7cc51\",\"name\":\"EDEN\",\"seating\":null,\"secondary_status\":null,\"new\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"EDEN, born Jonathon Ng in Dublin, Ireland, is an artist who defies traditional genre boundaries, blending electronic, indie, and alternative elements into a deeply personal soundscape. Emerging from the digital underground in the mid-2010s, EDEN first gained traction through self-released EPs End Credits (2015) and i think you think too much of me(2016), which collectively reached almost one billion streams worldwide and started to garner mass popularity for him in the scene.\\n\\nHis music, characterized by atmospheric textures, glitchy beats, and layered vocals, often explores themes of identity, mental health, and the complexities of modern life like in his debut album, vertigo (2018), which was lauded for its raw, introspective lyrics and innovative production.\\n\\nAs he continues to evolve, EDEN remains a unique force in contemporary music, challenging listeners to engage with his art on a deeper, more emotional level moving into his latest project Dark (2025) set to release this coming summer. The project displays a newly found optimism with the idea that some things that feel so intense are out of your hands, and the only way to live with it is to take the weight off your shoulders and find the beauty around you. A long awaited finale unfolding, Dark holds an early 2020’s border-less inspiration, effervescently smashing and cutting into itself leaving behind only a moment’s memory.\\n\\nStanding 14+, Balcony 8+ U14s accompanied\\n\\nUnder 25’s require ID to purchase alcohol\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"Standing 14+, Balcony 8+ U14s accompanied\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-08-19T15:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-03-12T18:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-08-22T10:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-03-12T19:00:00+00:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-03-12T23:00:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"EDEN - Ghost in the Shell\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2a4mF1ECLXfgpBQekwQZW5\",\"artist\":\"EDEN\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/f12b0baca092f97eed097c8bf53a8cb2fbbc5856?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"Ghost in the Shell\"},{\"type\":\"apple_music\",\"title\":\"EDEN - Ghost in the Shell\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/ghost-in-the-shell/1822309141?i=1822309152&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"EDEN\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview211/v4/76/71/2a/76712a7c-5b1b-665d-8839-d06b1818c0c6/mzaf_8111051998168993902.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"Ghost in the Shell\"}],\"score\":0,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"event_tag\":null},{\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Liane Carroll\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"123829\",\"about\"