ow_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"seating\":{\"region\":\"eu\",\"seats_io_event_id\":\"1417a6a1-ce2f-4cd8-a9c3-cdf25dccdce8\",\"seats_io_public_key\":\"97a3faa5-6221-44a1-af86-3a7773a7248c\",\"seat_selection\":\"enabled\"},\"about\":{\"description\":\"**The Swiss-Palestinian drummer and composer plays music exploring how migration has influenced jazz today.**\\n\\nThe Montreux Jazz Artists Foundation (MJAF) is a recognized non-profit foundation that supports the next generation of artists and encourages exchanges through the universal language of music. It pursues two core objectives: discovering and nurturing talented musicians in the early stages of their careers and making music accessible to all.\\n\\nRamzi Hammad is a Swiss-Palestinian drummer and composer from Zurich, Switzerland. His music merges influences from Arabic music, hip-hop and the London jazz scene to create a vibrant, urban and rhythmic soundworld completely his own.\\n\\nThe ticket price includes a £2 venue restoration levy.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is a 14+ event.\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Southbank Centre.\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"impression_id\":\"67e592f56c886db9:8\",\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/M1b6b467bf09?dice_id=M1b6b467bf09\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Q7e9b4509d43?dice_id=Q7e9b4509d43\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/h4534fcf5bb5?dice_id=h4534fcf5bb5\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Fe2cd4e4e3ff?dice_id=Fe2cd4e4e3ff\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/k0f0768af57c?dice_id=k0f0768af57c\",\"post_