cb67027?dice_id=Re276cb67027\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Rac721a607d6?dice_id=Rac721a607d6\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/I4b86401c940?dice_id=I4b86401c940\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Ob9441a24d62?dice_id=Ob9441a24d62\"},\"perm_name\":\"v3gp6g-bremermccoy-29th-mar-earth-london-tickets\",\"secondary_status\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-13/aee7e3a3-fbc8-4bf1-83cf-e8101a86535a.jpg?rect=528%2C0%2C2075%2C2075\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-13/aee7e3a3-fbc8-4bf1-83cf-e8101a86535a.jpg?rect=0%2C99%2C3130%2C1878\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-13/aee7e3a3-fbc8-4bf1-83cf-e8101a86535a.jpg?rect=995%2C0%2C1141%2C2075\"},\"properties\":[],\"about\":{\"description\":\"This event will take place in EartH Theatre.\\n\\nBremer/McCoy have, against all odds, created their own subdued cosmos in a noisy era. Their sixth album, “Kosmos”, captures the intimate and immediate atmosphere of their live shows, where songs can emerge in a moment or develop over years, and audiences can connect with the music — and with each other — without words.\\n\\nFor more information on access at EartH, please see our FAQs here: https://bit.ly/44dzl75 or contact us at access@earthackney.co.uk\\n\\nEartH is a social enterprise committed to supporting new musicians, with music studios in the venue that are completely free for young artists to use. When you attend a show in EartH Theatre, head to the back of the space to rent a cushion for just £2. Not only will you get to sit more comfortably, but all proceeds go towards funding Studio 36. Find out more here: https://earthackney.co.uk/about/studio-36/\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"16+ event. (16-17 with a responsible adult 18+,1:1) \",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"id\":\"69160cd22d3b060001d87e60\",\"name\":\"Bremer/McCoy\",\