Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-12-10T16:30:00+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-04-14T22:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-12-10T16:30:00+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-04-14T19:30:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-04-14T22:30:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"announcement_date_unix\":1765384200,\"offers_extras\":false,\"secondary_status\":null,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":0},\"id\":\"6939a323568a7c0001945f09\",\"name\":\"Winter McQuinn + Jules Smith + Birds Flying Backwards\",\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Winter McQuinn\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-27/eaba11e4-b6de-4771-a795-c156f1f6eee9.jpg?rect=147%2C0%2C580%2C580\"},\"artist_id\":\"115706\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"new\":false,\"seating\":null,\"perm_name\":\"nvwn3q-winter-mcquinn-jules-smith-birds-flying-backwards-14th-apr-the-old-blue-last-london-tickets\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-11/6e16df70-7dae-4973-bd67-38764e7d7102.jpg?rect=220%2C0%2C880%2C880\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-11/6e16df70-7dae-4973-bd67-38764e7d7102.jpg?rect=0%2C44%2C1320%2C792\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-11/6e16df70-7dae-4973-bd67-38764e7d7102.jpg?rect=418%2C0%2C484%2C880\"},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"score\":0,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Outfit x Summer of Psych presents: Winter McQuinn + Jules Smith + Birds Flying Backwards\\n\\n\\\\--\\nNaarm/Melbourne songwriter, Winter McQuinn explores country and folk, imbued by psychedelia with a contemporary edge.\\n\\nUK’s Shindig Magazine best-described McQuinn’s music as “pollinated with dashes of 21st Century environmentalism and political awareness.” His music ripples with free-ness similar to revered 1960s/70s artists such as Nick Drake and Syd Barrett, and contemporary artists such as Kate Bollinger, Tex Crick and Alex Izenberg. McQuinn’s 2021 debut album ‘A Rabble Of Bees’ marked the beginning of his solo wanderings into psychedelic outsider pop. His 2024 sophomore album ‘Move To The Trees’ (featured in Rolling Stone AU and KEXP’s ‘Best Of’ lists for 2024), saw McQuinn honing his craft with a series of anthems for the future, settled in post-psych folk and 70s soft rock energy.\\n\\nThe end of 2024 saw McQuinn release a co-written EP ‘Recently I’ve Been Missing The Colour Green’ with Acacia Pip (Pinch Points) which was described as “collection of 6 pastoral, slacker folk gems” by Shindig Magazine (UK), and lead to tours in Australia, Europe and the UK. McQuinn has also begun releasing music with a new duo project Beefheart and McQuinn with UK Artist Moby Beefheart (aka William Murray from outfit FUR).  \\n\\\\--\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"donation\":null,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"faqs\":[],\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":1175,\"name\":\"Kilimanjaro Live Limited\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://myticket.co.uk/privacy-policy\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Never Felt A Love Like This (with Hook N Sling) [feat. Dotan]\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/4rVVzAmIoBsqYXNsWeiGhg\",\"artist\":\"\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/0f5