-a25c-d913c2dfc64f.jpg?rect=0%2C86%2C3375%2C3375\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/5a52e2bc-7399-4423-a25c-d913c2dfc64f.jpg?rect=0%2C1097%2C3375%2C2025\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/5a52e2bc-7399-4423-a25c-d913c2dfc64f.jpg?rect=528%2C0%2C2320%2C4219\"},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"score\":0,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Bradley Jago is presenting his highly anticipated second EP 'My Inner Vitriol'; following his debut EP 'Girl Problems' - 2024. Join Bradley Jago and guests for a night of queer soul for queer souls.\\n\\nBradley Jago is a London-based artist and performer whose music blends the warmth of classic soul with the infectious hooks of modern pop. Proclaiming his music as ‘queer soul for queer souls’, Jago’s discography is routinely dark, vulnerable and cinematic, as he moves seamlessly between heartfelt ballads, sleek pop, and soaring neo-soul anthems. Having grown up and begun his early music career in Portsmouth, Jago’s discography is unwaveringly autobiographical, as he documents his journey from navigating queer identity in a conservative city to discovering freedom and self-expression within London’s creative landscape. Channelling influences from Adele and Amy Winehouse to Sam Smith and Leon Bridges, Jago is on a mission to centre queerness within the modern soul landscape, as he offers up intricate, nuanced stories that come with queer experiences.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"donation\":null,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"faqs\":[],\"marketeers\":[],\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"The Babes - Tomorrow Seems So Far Away\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5b5K1PHN1pfe