d_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"secondary_status\":null,\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"impression_id\":\"ab902a79f4685193:34\",\"about\":{\"description\":\"Post-punk band **Radiator** return to London after touring their debut EP 'Glass'.\\n\\nAfter being championed by the likes of Steve Lamacq and tastemaker magazine Still Listening, the group hit the Top 40 of the Official Vinyl Singles Chart in December.\\n\\nWith a host of festival dates lined up, and a BBC Introducing live session in the pipeline, Radiator will be marking the release of their first new music of 2026 with this gig.\\n\\nSupport comes from:\\n\\n**\\\\- irisworm**: Inspired by the Thames Valley scene of the late 80s/early 90s, irisworm brings to light a revival of shoegaze and dream pop. With her use of lush soundscapes and wispy vocals, irisworm blends the sounds of British shoegaze with overseas influences such as Drop Nineteens and Mazzy Star.\\n\\n@iriswor.m\\n\\n**\\\\- The Draize**: South London’s latest janglegaze four piece, The Draize, ushers itself back into the sonic mess with a new crew. Drenched in reverberated jangle and feedback, we’re lost in the swirl, but chasing something honest.\\n\\n@thedraizeband\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"seating\":null,\"announcement_date_unix\":1769385600,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"donation\":null,\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Radiator\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"125884\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":2},\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-26/85b37df3-b424-4cfd-ba9a-4b9b23fdb07a.jpg?rect=113%2C0%2C768%2C7