tter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"secondary_status\":null,\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"impression_id\":\"ab902a79f4685193:55\",\"about\":{\"description\":\"After the jubilee year of 2025 — which for Nocny Kochanek looked like an attempt to break the record for the number of projects squeezed into twelve months — the band has no intention of slowing down or looking back. After arena shows, cinematic adventures, planting trees in their hometown of Skarżysko-Kamienna, and releasing a cookbook in collaboration with SQN Publishing, the Traitors of Metal are hitting the road again — this time beyond the borders of Poland.\\n\\nThe concert setlist will cover material from the entire history of Nocny Kochanek: tracks from the debut album Hewi Metal, songs from Zdrajcy Metalu, Randka w Ciemność, O Jeden Most za Daleko, and finally from the conceptual Urwany film. And of course, there will be no shortage of songs from the compilation As w nogawce!\\n\\nMusically, Nocny Kochanek delivers heavy metal inspired by the giants of the genre — something you can hear at first… ear. The lyrics feature the band’s signature Night Lover–style humor and are usually based on facts, sometimes even real ones..! Using comedy rooted in pastiche, wordplay, and absurdity, Nocny Kochanek paints a portrait of the Polish metal subculture with a huge dose of self‑distance and a playful approach to the image typically associated with classic heavy metal.\\n\\nIf the jubilee year proved that the band can do absolutely anything, this spring tour is meant to show that they still do it best when they’re on stage\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"seating\":null,\"announcement_date_unix\":1769558400,\