round-london-tickets\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/f61ddffa-6be5-46d5-8150-9d8cad889ab2.jpg?rect=584%2C0%2C3107%2C3107\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/f61ddffa-6be5-46d5-8150-9d8cad889ab2.jpg?rect=0%2C271%2C4275%2C2565\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/f61ddffa-6be5-46d5-8150-9d8cad889ab2.jpg?rect=1283%2C0%2C1709%2C3107\"},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"score\":0,\"about\":{\"description\":\"Katie Tupper’s music is led by her deep alto voice and blends soul, indie, alternative, and R&B. Born in Saskatoon, Saskatchewan, Tupper's two previous EPs of heartland soul–Towards The End (2022), and Where To Find Me (2023)–have amassed 22 million streams worldwide and a JUNO Award nomination. She’s had a meteoric rise on social media with over 40 million views across short form platforms and now she’s heading into 2026 with her debut album, Greyhound, in hand. This album is a homecoming, a return to her roots with years of new experience. It embraces the expanse of the endless sky and the light of the golden fields with an undercurrent of the sidewalks and skylines she’s spent years calling home. \\n\\nIf you have any queries or would like more information about access at Village Underground, please see our FAQs here: https://bit.ly/3EhSLgF, or contact access@villageunderground.co.uk.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"16+ event. (16-17 with a responsible adult 18+,1:1) \",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"donation\":null,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"faqs\":[],\"marketeers\":[],\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"previews\":[],\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"properties\":[],\"date_unix\"