00:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-05-20T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"announcement_date_unix\":1770303600,\"offers_extras\":false,\"secondary_status\":null,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":3499},\"id\":\"6983771595ad180001aab67f\",\"name\":\"The Lemon Twigs\",\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"The Lemon Twigs\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/9b3bde80-d672-4079-af0b-99d5fe47a2d7.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C640%2C640\"},\"artist_id\":\"3031\",\"about\":{\"description\":\"As theatrical as they are referential, The Lemon Twigs are indie rock brother duo Brian and Michael D’Addario. Based in Long Island, the pair’s vintage sound (and look) takes cues from the baroque rock, glam rock and power pop of the ’60s and ’70s. On 2020’s Songs for the General Public, the brothers “gleefully joust with rock’s macho past” (Pitchfork), while in their live performances they flaunt their innate charisma and flamboyance across the stage.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"new\":false,\"seating\":null,\"perm_name\":\"oevkdy-the-lemon-twigs-20th-may-o2-shepherds-bush-empire-london-tickets\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/2f580586-c46b-4ea9-8a93-a1e814187e76.jpg?rect=216%2C0%2C849%2C849\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/2f580586-c46b-4ea9-8a93-a1e814187e76.jpg?rect=0%2C41%2C1280%2C768\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-04/2f580586-c46b-4ea9-8a93-a1e814187e76.jpg?rect=407%2C0%2C467%2C849\"},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"score\":0,\"about\":{\"description\":\"The Lemon Twigs, the New York City rock band fronted by brothers Brian and Michael D’Addario, have been steadily capturing attention with their unique blend of youthful energy and seasoned songwriting. Drawing on nearly a decade of experience since theirdebut as teenagers, they combine rock, California harmony, power pop and baroque pop into a distinctive, joyously inventive sound. Their work is marked by intricate arrangements, multilayered harmonies, and adventurous instrumentation –all self-produced in their Brooklyn studio. The brothers craft songs that balance escapist pop with moments of introspection, seamlessly shifting between styles while communicating their ideas with emotional resonance, setting them apart in modern rock music.\\n\\nNo under 8s. Under 14s must be accompanied by an adult over 18 years old at all times and seated in the balcony.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"donation\":null,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"faqs\":[{\"id\":72779,\"title\":\"Venue Restoration Levy\",\"body\":\"The restoration levy is £1.20 for 229.\",\"order\":0}],\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":294,\"name\":\"229 The Venue\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://229.london/dataprotection/\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"previews\":[],\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"properties\":[],\"date_unix\":1779300000,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"399\",\"name\":\"229\",\"address\":\"229 Great Portland St, London W1W 5PN, UK\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.523568,\"lng\":-0.144821},\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2022-04-28/84389ecd-ecb4-45bc-a846-5cf9964535ff.jpg?rect=180%2C0%2C838%2C838\"},\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d