tists\":0,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"new\":false,\"announcement_date_unix\":1764669600,\"faqs\":[],\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":1683,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"seating\":null,\"previews\":[],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-10-07T00:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-05-22T00:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-10-07T00:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-05-23T19:00:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-05-23T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"presented_by\":\"Presented by AGMP.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"properties\":[],\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"offers_extras\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/s114bcdd483f?dice_id=s114bcdd483f\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/ya017605b94b?dice_id=ya017605b94b\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Ze6569db0031?dice_id=Ze6569db0031\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Jfee5759c8cb?dice_id=Jfee5759c8cb\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/f6b0483d075e?dice_id=f6b0483d075e\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/e3b7633996fe?dice_id=e3b7633996fe\"},\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"CLEARWATER CREEDENCE REVIVAL + TEN YEARS AFTER\\n\\n‘Fortunate Son’ Tour\\n\\n**Creedence Clearwater Revival** are one of the most iconic rock groups of all time. Their all time classic hits such as Proud Mary, Bad Moon Rising, Have You Ever Seen The Rain, Born on the Bayou, Fortunate Son, Down on the Corner, Up Around the Bend along with CCR and John Fogerty fan favourites are powerfully reprised by Clearwater Creedence Revival.\\n\\nPETER BARTON – vocals, guitar\\n\\nALAN SAGAR – bass\\n\\nJIM KIRKPATRICK – guitar\\n\\nGEOFF HAMMOND – drums\\n\\n**Ten Years After** are celebrated for timeless classics including I’m Going Home, Love Like A Man, Hear Me Calling, I’d Love To Change The World, and Let The Sky Fall, alongside four UK Top 10 albums – Stonedhenge, Undead, Ssssh, and Cricklewood Green. Their legendary performance at Woodstock in 1969 secured their place as one of the era’s most influential rock bands.\\n\\nRIC LEE - Drums\\n\\nSAMUEL C. LEES - Guitar/Vocals\\n\\nCRAIG FLETCHER - Bass/Vocals\\n\\nDAVE BURGOYNE - keyboards\\n\\nAn AGMP Concerts presentation.\\n\\nPlease note: Clearwater Creedence Revival are a tribute to the music of.C.C.R and John Fogerty and not the original band.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"16+\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"marketeers\":[],\"date_unix\":1779559200,\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"460\",\"name\":\"Indigo at The O2\",\"address\":\"The O2, Peninsula Square, London SE10 0DX\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5025248,\"lng\":0.00366410000003725},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"indigo-at-the-o2-jqlo\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.theo2.co.uk/visit-us/accessibility#indigo\"},\"profile_active\":false,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-05-23T19:00:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"max_tickets\":6,\"donation\":null,\"streaming_options\":null,\"impression_id\":\"3775695cf81d3a40:59\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"secondary_status\":null,\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"1442\",\"name\":\"AGMP\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"agmp-99g9\",\"profile_active\":false},\"id\":\"68f1046396f243000177054b\",\"name\":\"Clearwater Creedence Revival + Ten Years After\",\"perm_name\":\"pypq9l-clearwater-creedence-revival-ten-years-after-23rd-may-indigo-at-the-o2-london-tickets\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-16/24eeb4d3-6ddb-4a4c-9139-849315958878.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C1080%2C1080\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-16/24eeb4d3-6ddb-4a4c-9139-849315958878.jpg?rect=0%2C216%2C1080%2C648\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-10-16/24eeb4d3-6ddb-4a4c-9139-849315958878.jpg?rect=243%2C0%2C594%2C1080\"},\"unicorn\":true,\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Ten Years After\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-i-scdn-co.imgix.net/image/2c825769bc2470bf5aaf04a5991db4612298c5dd\"},\"artist_id\":\"35801\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Clearwater Creedence Revival (Peter Barton)\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"43484\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":2,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"new\":false,\"announcement_date_unix\":1759791600,\"faqs\":[{\"id\":51207,\"title\":\"What's the bag policy?\",\"body\":\"Security – Bag Policy\\n\\nLarge bags – including rucksacks are not allowed.\\n\\nThere are no facilities to leave large bags or luggage.\\n\\nIf you really have to bring a bag – and it’s preferable you don’t – please make sure it’s small.\\n\\nOnly one small bag per person is permitted and it must not be bigger than A4 size.\\n\\nHeight: 28.7cm\\n\\nWidth: 21cm\\n\\nDepth 15cm\",\"order\":0}],\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":4150,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"seating\":null,\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"I'd Love to Change the World - 2004 Remaster\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/19HjHUjCfDrEYhVSIKG6nK\",\"artist\":\"I'd Love to Change the World\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/5e41b1797524070cc373c6d6b44577916085079f?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"2004 Remaster\"}],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-10-15T14:45:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-05-22T15:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-10-24T10:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-05-23T19:00:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-05-23T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"presented_by\":\"Presented by DHP FAMILY.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"properties\":[],\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"offers_extras\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Ac94e9baa6a9?dice_id=Ac94e9baa6a9\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/fb16ebffc59e?dice_id=fb16ebffc59e\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Lb4ba496d663?dice_id=Lb4ba496d663\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/K68e8eb4aa76?dice_id=K68e8eb4aa76\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/K6dc02472c51?dice_id=K6dc02472c51\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r1234c5c2a61?dice_id=r1234c5c2a61\"},\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"about\":{\"description\":\"DHP Presents:\\n\\nSugar\\n\\n\\\\+ support\\n\\nHaving already placed his indelible mark on the future direction of rock with Hüsker Dü, Bob Mould teamed with bassist David Barbe and drummer Malcolm Travis to found Sugar in late 1991, making their live debut early the next year at Athens, GA’s famed 40 Watt Club. Named by NME as its 1992 “Album of the Year,” Sugar’s now-classic debut album, Copper Blue, immediately proved a sensation, earning worldwide acclaim and landmark status for the melodic strength and intensely cathartic popcraft of songs like “A Good Idea,” “Helpless,” and the alternative rock radio hit and MTV favorite, “If I Can’t Change Your Mind.” The trio quickly found themselves performing on increasingly larger stages, including a legendary show-stealing set at London’s Great X-pectations Festival in Finsbury Park.\\n\\nWith the wind at their back, Sugar unleashed Beaster in 1993, making a momentous debut at #3 on the UK’s Official Albums Chart as well as at #4 on Billboard’s “Heatseekers” chart in the US. Though recorded during the same sessions that yielded Copper Blue, the six-song mini-album evinced a more visceral energy and dark melancholy than its predecessor, highlighted by such pulverizing expressions of sacrilegious fury as “Judas Cradle” and “JC Auto.” 1994’s second full-length LP, File Under: Easy Listening once again made an explosive arrival among the top 10 on the UK Official Albums Chart, this time landing in the upper reaches of the overall Billboard 200. The album saw Sugar pushing boundaries yet again on songs like the country-flavored “Believe What You’re Saying” and the incendiary “Gee Angel,” tackling a wider range of musical approaches without sacrificing their signature intensity and unrestrained power. Despite their successes, Sugar called it a day following a Japanese tour in early 1995. A series of live recordings, reissues, and anthologies served to magnify the band’s legacy over the three decades since, confirming Sugar as incontrovertible masters of high-volume guitar-fueled rock for the ages. \\n\\nThe original members of Sugar reconvened in June 2025. The first new song in over three decades, “House Of Dead Memories”, was released on October 15, 2025, with live shows to follow in 2026.\\n\\nThis price includes a £2.50 venue restoration levy.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 8+ event (Under 14's to be accompanied by an adult)\"