ple_music\",\"title\":\"Ruins - Outburn\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/outburn/1082764740?i=1082764745&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"Ruins\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview115/v4/9f/63/dc/9f63dc90-b3e6-d6c4-b970-d97ea091783c/mzaf_17723346422434536060.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"Outburn\"}],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":1500,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Other Side Promotions.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"faqs\":[],\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"5285\",\"name\":\"Other Side Promotions\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2021-09-09/c8464497-8f12-4558-84bb-ede11bc2ddb5.jpg\"},\"perm_name\":\"other-side-promotions-r5gv\",\"profile_active\":true},\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"perm_name\":\"q2893o-dope-purple-twn-black-tempest-deviant-amps-10th-jun-strongroom-bar-london-tickets\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"secondary_status\":null,\"date_unix\":1781117100,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"max_tickets\":6,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"impression_id\":\"8fa9a59af65bb1b7:16\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"298\",\"name\":\"Strongroom Bar\",\"address\":\"120-124 Curtain Rd, Shoreditch, London EC2A 3SQ, UK\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5259644,\"lng\":-0.0801498},\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2021-11-09/01c2cab5-15ea-48e0-a0b4-d9ed0465d9db.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C850%2C850\"},\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"strongroom-bar-4bym\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":null},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-06-10T19:45:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Deviant Amps\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"97406\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Black Tempest\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"104360\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Dope Purple\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"133798\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":3,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"about\":{\"description\":\"**Dope Purple (TWN):**\\n\\nDope Purple are a psychedelic/noise rock band formed in Taipei in 2016, who channel influences from hard rock, noise & psychedelia with a particular emphasis on sounds from the Japanese underground, into a cosmic guitar explosion.\\n\\nDope Purple champion Taiwan's psych rock culture & hosts the Taipei Psychedelic Rock Music Festival, inviting musicians like Makoto Kawabata (Acid Mother Temple) & Taigen Kawabe (Bo Ningen). Dope Purple has also been actively touring worldwide to critical acclaim.\\n\\nIn 2025, WV Sorcerer Productions (FR) & Riot Season Records (UK) jointly released new album 'Children in the Darkness'.\\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/dope_purple_band/\\n\\nhttps://wvsorcerer.bandcamp.com/album/children-in-the-darkness\\n\\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@DopePurple666\\n\\n**Black Tempest:**\\n\\nBlack Tempest is Surrey-based multi-instrumentalist Stephen Bradbury.\\n\\nKnown for his deeply psychedelic synth epics, he has released 3 albums on the Weird Beard label - Psyberspace, Psyborg & Astral Pastoral. He also collaborated with Manchester's Dead Sea Apes & has appeared at the Supernormal Festival, the Glastonbury Psych Fest, & supported Gnod on the main London date of their European tour in 2024.\\n\\nhttps://blacktempest.bandcamp.com/music\\n\\n**Deviant Amps:**\\n\\nDeviant Amps were formed in the UK in 1983. They produce full on psychedelic freak out songs which are influenced by 60’s and 70’s psych & 70’s spacerock, with nods to modern psych bands.\\n\\nhttps://linktr.ee/deviantamps\\n\\nThis is an 18+ event. This venue has a strict No ID, No entry Policy. Physical government photo ID required, we do not accept photos or copies of ID’s.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"seating\":null,\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-06-10T18:30:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-06-10T19:45:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-06-10T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"properties\":[],\"id\":\"698a33bef17f400001a89388\",\"name\":\"Dope Purple (TWN) + Black Tempest + Deviant Amps\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-09/576241df-a340-4ae1-9c8b-c7239cd1d6d9.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C2160%2C2160\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-09/576241df-a340-4ae1-9c8b-c7239cd1d6d9.jpg?rect=0%2C432%2C2160%2C1296\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-09/576241df-a340-4ae1-9c8b-c7239cd1d6d9.jpg?rect=486%2C0%2C1188%2C2160\"},\"marketeers\":[],\"new\":false,\"offers_extras\":false,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"announcement_date_unix\":1770665400,\"donation\":null,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Y324a1e6f66e?dice_id=Y324a1e6f66e\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/ca0d701f75b2?dice_id=ca0d701f75b2\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/T18a74040756?dice_id=T18a74040756\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/R004ba410996?dice_id=R004ba410996\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/K6bc949e5077?dice_id=K6bc949e5077\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/I505b4a03c50?dice_id=I505b4a03c50\"},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Dope Purple - My Evilness\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/5ISjsy6F0jsY5nnluMJCCq\",\"artist\":\"Dope Purple\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/9aac2b5794ab41dd45698af3ce7513d60e4d464b?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"My Evilness\"},{\"type\":\"apple_music\",\"title\":\"Dope Purple - My Evilness\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/my-evilness/1602318370?i=1602318378&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"Dope Purple\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview116/v4/32/12/2e/32122e8a-3ae8-7fc1-c9d0-ee28c363b7ae/mzaf_9344903620864824734.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"My Evilness\"}],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null}],\"title\":\"Wed 10 Jun\",\"image\":null,\"key\":null,\"action\":null,\"subtitle\":null,\"suggestion_type\":null,\"suggestion_name\":null,\"section_type\":\"events_vertical\",\"load_more\":null,\"section_hash\":null},{\"events\":[{\"unicorn\":false,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":6889},\"seats_io_public_key\":\"91b87c00-af06-457c-b5e8-4d8f0af2ae7f\",\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Communion ONE.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"faqs\":[{\"id\":48501,\"title\":\"FAQs for The O2\",\"body\":\"Further information about visiting The O2 can be found at https://help.theo2.co.uk/hc/en-gb\",\"order\":0},{\"id\":48502,\"title\":\"How to book accessible tickets for The O2\",\"body\":\"Accessible Seating Accessible bookings can be purchased online when selecting the event via www.theo2.co.uk and visiting the https://www.theo2.co.uk/visit-us/accessibility, DICE do not process any Accessible tickets for any event at The O2.\",\"order\":1},{\"id\":48503,\"title\":\"How tickets work for The O2\",\"body\":\"Tickets will be in The O2 venue app as they’re handling ticket scanning for this event. We will email you when your tickets are available in the app.\\n\\nHow to use your tickets:\\n\\n1\\\\. Get The O2 venue app - https://www.theo2.co.uk/visit-us/the-o2-app\\n\\n2\\\\. Sign up using the email you used to purchase your tickets on DICE\\n\\n3\\\\. At the door, show your tickets on the venue app (not DICE)\",\"order\":2},{\"id\":48504,\"title\":\"Can I change my seat?\",\"body\":\"Seats can’t be changed after booking, so please review your selection carefully before checkout.\",\"order\":3}],\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"14302\",\"name\":\"Communion ONE\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"communion-one-bbl7g\",\"profile_active\":true},\"seats_io_event_id\":\"a397ef06-313e-46af-be4b-a37ce25af8d4\",\"perm_name\":\"q2adw9-olivia-dean-11th-jun-the-o2-london-london-tickets\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"secondary_status\":\"waiting-list\",\"date_unix\":1781199000,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_disabled\"},\"status\":\"sold-out\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"max_tickets\":6,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"impression_id\":\"8fa9a59af65bb1b7:17\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"584\",\"name\":\"The O2, London\",\"address\":\"O2 Arena\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5025248,\"lng\":0.00366410000003725},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"the-o2-london-q2xy\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":null},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-06-11T18:30:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Olivia Dean\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-22/0f34a8d2-2acd-4aa9-a2bd-6c2993f875db.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C1200%2C1200\"},\"artist_id\":\"13260\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"about\":{\"description\":\"Standing: Over 16s only. Seated: Under 16s must be accompanied by an adult over 18.\\n\\nOlivia Dean has partnered with PLUS1 so that £1 (+ VAT) per ticket goes to supporting the LIVE Trust (Charity Number: 1211251) and their work supporting those who are keeping venues open, festivals trading, artists touring and all those involved in the promoting and staging of live music performances.\\n\\nThere is a £3.25 Venue Facility Fee included in the ticket price.\\n\\nAccessible Seating Accessible bookings can be purchased online when selecting the event via www.theo2.co.uk and visiting the https://www.theo2.co.uk/visit-us/accessibility, DICE do not process any Accessible tickets for any event at The O2.\\n\\nOlivia Dean’s highly anticipated sophomore album The Art of Loving went straight in at #1 on the UK album charts, alongside hit single ‘Man I Need’ which also peaked at #1 in the UK singles chart - becoming the first solo British Female artist to claim the #1 single & #1 album simultaneously since Adele in 2021. Olivia also announced two more dates for her residency at The O2 in London on the 11th & 12th of June, adding to her biggest ever UK and EU tour, which kicks off in April 2026. Tickets for the new dates are available here: https://link.dice.fm/x2e53627ec0d\\n\\nThe tour will commence at Glasgow’s OVO Hydro on April 23rd, before embarking cross-country and culminating in six huge shows at The O2 in London - including four in April / May and two new additional nights in June as part of her O2 residency. Olivia also takes her exceptional live show across Europe performing tracks from The Art of Loving as well as live favourites off her Mercury Prize nominated debut, Messy.\\n\\nSpeaking on her chart success, Olivia said: “I feel very grateful and overwhelmed! I love the album I made and I’m so proud of myself for making it. But ultimately it is so joyful seeing how much it means to people and how it’s helping people understand love and loving.”\\n\\nOlivia currently also holds three of the top 10 biggest British singles released in 2025 so far, as well as The Art of Loving garnering the biggest opening week for a British female artist since Adele in 2021, according to Official Charts. The record, which includes fan favourites ‘Nice To Each Other’ and lead single ‘So Easy (To Fall In Love)’, quickly rose to Number 1 on the Official Albums Chart, and hit single ‘Man I Need’ became the highest charting song from a UK act on Spotify’s Global Charts this year, as well as charting at #25 (to date) on the Billboard Hot 100. The Art of Loving has since become the fastest selling album for a British female artist in 2025.\\n\\nStanding: Over 16s only. Seated: Under 16s must be accompanied by an adult over 18.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"seating\":{\"region\":\"eu\",\"seats_io_event_id\":\"a397ef06-313e-46af-be4b-a37ce25af8d4\",\"seats_io_public_key\":\"91b87c00-af06-457c-b5e8-4d8f0af2ae7f\",\"seat_selection\":\"enabled\"},\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-10-03T18:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-06-11T15:30:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-10-10T10:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-06-11T18:30:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"properties\":[],\"id\":\"68dff27d756ff50001cc756e\",\"name\":\"Olivia Dean\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/4b0085a1-4147-460d-83eb-7b26310de973.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C1200%2C1200\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/4b0085a1-4147-460d-83eb-7b26310de973.jpg?rect=0%2C240%2C1200%2C720\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-08-21/4b0085a1-4147-460d-83eb-7b26310de973.jpg?rect=270%2C0%2C660%2C1200\"},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":191,\"name\":\"Olivia Dean (via Universal Music)\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.umusic.co.uk/privacy.html\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false},{\"id\":2127,\"name\":\"The O2, London\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.theo2.co.uk/legal/privacy\",\"fb_pixel_id\":null,\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_conversion_label\":null,\"show_web_opt_in_form\":true,\"show_opt_in_form\":true,\"opt_out_as_default\":false}],\"new\":false,\"offers_extras\":false,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"announcement_date_unix\":1759510800,\"donation\":null,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/e0cc60d9b246?dice_id=e0cc60d9b246\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Ud53d15c0c56?dice_id=Ud53d15c0c56\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Id454e431175?dice_id=Id454e431175\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/d6b443adada0?dice_id=d6b443adada0\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/W8f13d2ecace?dice_id=W8f13d2ecace\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/te45cc2f49c8?dice_id=te45cc2f49c8\"},\"unicorn_extras\":false,\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Danger\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/1zAITH7C5UFYNE8DOFlE7h\",\"artist\":\"\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/54a534c34e5c124540cc1463d2cb36e3674e9833?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"Danger\"}],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":3760,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by The Underworld.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"faqs\":[{\"id\":74744,\"title\":\"Offer your ticket to another fan\",\"body\":\"We believe tickets belong in the hands of fans, and that they should only ever be sold for a fair price. That’s why we have the Waiting List: if you can’t make it to a sold-out event, you can add your ticket to the queue to be purchased by another fan. If the ticket is sold, you’ll get your money back – no drama, no rip-offs.\\n\\nThere are a few conditions, though. Not every show will have the Waiting List function switched on, and tickets can only be added to the Waiting List after a show sells out. On top of that – and this is important – you’ll only get your money back if another fan buys your ticket.\\n\\nLearn more about how the Waiting List works https://dice.fm/help/article?id=4409669479953\",\"order\":0},{\"id\":74745,\"title\":\"Transfer your ticket to a friend \",\"body\":\"If a friend is keen to attend an event you can’t make, you can transfer your ticket to them quickly and securely within the app. Just make sure you have their number saved in your phone, and that they have a DICE account registered with that number.\\n\\nAfter you transfer the ticket, it will be stored within the DICE app on your friend’s phone – there’s no fiddling with name changes, emailing PDFs, or sending across screenshots. It’s just another way we make sure tickets don’t fall into the wrong hands.\\n\\nThe whole process takes seconds, here’s a step-by-step breakdown https://dice.fm/help/article?id=4409669378449\",\"order\":1},{\"id\":74746,\"title\":\"Can I purchase tickets from a third-party ticket website?\",\"body\":\"DICE does not participate in re-selling with any third-party sites as our tickets are only accessible via our app using the unique QR code that can only be activated on the day of the event.\\n\\nYou will be rejected at the door, if you show a ticket from third-party ticket resale site.\\n\\nOur wait list feature puts fans first and ensures they aren’t being charged more than the actual ticket price. The wait list is the only way to ensure you are purchasing a genuine ticket that will give you entry into your favourite events!\",\"order\":2}],\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"52\",\"name\":\"The Underworld\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"the-underworld-zkx8\",\"profile_active\":false},\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"perm_name\":\"2w8rk7-drain-11th-jun-the-underworld-london-tickets\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"secondary_status\":\"waiting-list\",\"date_unix\":1781200800,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"status\":\"sold-out\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"max_tickets\":6,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"impression_id\":\"8fa9a59af65bb1b7:18\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"53\",\"name\":\"The Underworld\",\"address\":\"174 Camden High St, London NW1 0NE\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5391426,\"lng\":-0.142163900000014},\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2022-07-25/f029c393-780a-492d-8c51-acec64197fc4.jpg?rect=391%2C0%2C1569%2C1569\"},\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"the-underworld-zg7p\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.theunderworldcamden.co.uk/about/\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00+01:00\"}],\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Pest Control\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2023-12-04/be453d32-a39e-40e4-a1d7-5ec62c5aaa85.jpg?rect=0%2C53%2C534%2C534\"},\"artist_id\":\"50681\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Higher Power\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2023-08-18/68405d7c-8d91-40f8-9533-424cd6a36c6b.jpg?rect=0%2C53%2C535%2C535\"},\"artist_id\":\"4962\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false},{\"name\":\"Drain\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-i-scdn-co.imgix.net/image/ab6761610000e5ebe3850e09ebed9df667c9f162\"},\"artist_id\":\"61766\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":true}],\"total_artists\":3,\"total_free_texts\":1},\"about\":{\"description\":\"“Straight up, no one is having more fun than me when we’re up there!” beams DRAIN frontman Sammy Ciaramitaro, whose face is perpetually glued in a grin. For anyone that’s seen the Santa Cruz hardcore firebrands live, there’s no mistaking that fact. Drain isn’t just a good time as Sammy presides over the chaos of stagediving bodies and mic-grabbing frontline; it’s a party—and everyone is invited. (Dolphin shorts and boogie boards are optional but encouraged.) “The vibe of it is, enthusiastic, hectic,” says the vocalist. “Five people deep singing and stagediving, then kids going berserk behind that. It’s a great vibe and I think people pick up on that.”\\n\\nThat, in a nutshell is DRAIN. The quartet inject a serious dose of relatability—not to mention catchiness—into hardcore’s penchant for toughness and brutality on their Epitaph debut Living Proof. Ciaramitaro’s desperate, snotty howl rides roughshod over thrash-leaning riffage as rhythms bounce in a big way. If you’re picturing the Pacific Ocean waves that rise and fall along the coastal town, occasionally violently so, you’re not far off.\\n\\nProduced by longtime friend and multi-instrumentalist Taylor Young (God’s Hate, Suicide Silence), then mixed by John Markson (Drug Church, Koyo), this is hardcore for everybody. “As the band gets bigger, I try and keep that feeling alive,” says the smiling singer. “Every night I set up the merch and run it until it’s time to play. I want to be the guy that everyone says hello to. I want to thank every single kid that comes out for being there.”\\n\\nFrom opener “Run Your Luck” to the closing title track, between surefire pit-pleaser “Imposter” to solo-charged anthem “Weight of the World,” Living Proof is a surefire spark-to-flame for a band that can’t help but be anything but themselves. “It’s very authentic, which is why kids can relate,” says Ciaramitaro. “I’m not a super deep, poetic lyricist. I want to feel like I’m having a conversation, very down to earth. I’m not going to front, I grew up middle-class; I grew up in a house, a suburban home. I’m not from the streets and I’m not going to front like I am. Lyrically, the things I write about are things I can personally attest to.”\\n\\nDRAIN came together in the sleepy, oceanside NorCal climes of Santa Cruz in 2014 when Ciaramitaro met up with guitarist Cody Chavez and drummer Tim Flegal while attending college. “We had no idea or gameplan of what we were trying to do,” says Sammy. “It was more like, ‘Hey, you have a metal band T-shirt, and I got a Downpresser shirt on, and someone likes Municipal Waste. We should all play together.’” While nearby scenes like San Jose and Oakland (known for the legendary Gilman Street venue) had local heat, Drain had to pull up their bootstraps to ignite their own. “We made our own scene in Santa Cruz,” reveals the DIY vocalist proudly; he began booking shows at Café Pergolesi, a local coffee shop that became the town’s hardcore hub.\\n\\n“When people come to Santa Cruz, they’re like, ‘Oh, I get it, DRAIN looks like what this town looks like. We also sound like what you expect Santa Cruz to sound like,” says the frontman, touching on their home’s penchant for surfing and skating. The quartet all grew up in California and proudly embrace its hardcore history. Ciaramitaro hails from the South Bay’s San Pedro, which birthed Black Flag and The Minutemen, a far cry from DRAIN’s sound but with an intensity and honesty they undeniably channel.\\n\\nIt’s the same kind of spirit that allowed them to build a Santa Cruz homebase and the same kind of spirit that would allow them to wave its flag across the nation on the back of two EPs: Over Thinking (2016) and Time Enough at Last (2017). It earned them pockets of fans across the United States, but it was with 2018’s promo single that DRAIN’s California cool started boiling over. The two songs (“Army of One” and “California Cursed”) were, simply put, AWESOME and these Beach Sharks shredded a blistering set at 2019’s Los Angeles’ Sound and Fury fest and rode the wave straight to a deal with Revelation Records.\\n\\nTheir debut for the label took its name, California Cursed, a little too literally when it launched at the dawn of Covid-19 and the resultant worldwide lockdown. Well, sort of—the smiley singer even found a blessing in that curse.\\n\\n“Kids fell in love with music but didn’t have the chance for two years to see it live,” states Sammy. “Now that it’s come back, the feeling is, ‘I want to see it live. I want to go to every show. I want to experience it.” DRAIN didn’t merely jump back onto stages across North American, they exploded onto them. The brunt of that force was felt at San Jose’s REAL BAY SHIT! show, a guerilla-styled seven-band assault at an industrial park on the outskirts of the town that had rapidly risen to become the epicenter of hardcore. DRAIN played direct support to Gulch, the metallic group in which Ciaramitaro also played drums before their refreshingly planned demise. Other sets came courtesy of Sunami, Xibalba, Scowl and more, resulting in the June 19, 2021 date going down in history for the over 2,000 show-starved attendees—nay, hardcore at large.\\n\\nDespite its large turnout, the landmark show’s origins were much more modest. “It doesn’t get more DIY than that, just a handful of us,” beams Sammy, who was one of the day’s organizers. “We built the stage ourselves. No promoters or big business. Just us on our social media sharing a flyer – it was a turning point for us.”\\n\\nAround the corner was a litany of good things for DRAIN, including the announcement of their signing with Epitaph Records. The process had begun much earlier, however, with the SoCal label getting in touch with the NorCal band a mere five days after California Cursed dropped. They inked a deal with the understanding that the signees would tour their recent release before even thinking about a follow-up album. And tour they would, hopping on the road for headline and one supporting Terror, as fans of the surging hardcore scene clamored for the Santa Cruz quartet’s brand of good, friendly violent fun.\\n\\nAfter hitting the studio to record Living Proof and then, making their live European debut, DRAIN headlined the first night of 2022’s landmark Sound and Fury festival playing to 6,000 kids keyed up to welcome the next generation of hardcore royalty.\\n\\n“We didn’t know we were headlining,” laughs Ciaramitaro, who also played the second night for Gulch’s fiery final show. “It was wild, totally surreal. It felt not real. We’ve kind of been the underdogs from day one: overlooked, too goofy, whatever. Flash forward six years, hey we’re headlining Sound and Fury. We really did this our own way which is crazy.”\\n\\nLiving Proof is just that. It’s a testament to the hard work and heartfelt ethos that’s at the center of DRAIN’s good-time psyche. There are a couple surprises on the album. Rapper Shakewell appears on the track, “Intermission”. “He’s a hardcore dude. He used to play in that band Betrayal,” reveals Ciaramitaro. There’s also a cover of “Good, Good Things,” a nearly four-decade old melodic punk carol by the Descendents: slam-pit forebearers to DRAIN if there ever were any. “It’s crazy because the song’s been out like forty years, but lyrically it’s a DRAIN song!” exclaims Sam. “It just hits on everything that I love, that I’m about.”\\n\\nWhat Sammy’s about is plenty wholesome. “I hope with this record that when someone hears it it gives them hope,” Ciaramitaro beams. “If we were able to get through the tough times, anyone can. I can’t wait to play these songs and hear a room full of people singing back to us. We’re what the title says, the Living Proof.”\\n\\nThis is a 14+ event. 14 and 15 year olds MUST be accompanied by an adult (18+) / All ticketholders under the age of 25 will be required to carry PHOTO ID.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"seating\":null,\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2026-02-10T10:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-06-11T17:30:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2026-02-12T10:00:00+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"properties\":[],\"id\":\"6985a5953c020000019bfbbd\",\"name\":\"DRAIN\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-10/00c12987-8e19-4f8f-a98d-4b74c5e28127.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C2400%2C2400\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-10/00c12987-8e19-4f8f-a98d-4b74c5e28127.jpg?rect=0%2C480%2C2400%2C1440\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-02-10/00c12987-8e19-4f8f-a98d-4b74c5e28127.jpg?rect=540%2C0%2C1320%2C2400\"},\"marketeers\":[{\"id\":21,\"name\":\"The Underworld\",\"privacy_policy_link\":\"https://www.theunderworldcamden.co.uk/privacy-policy/\",\"fb_pixel_id\":\"1396572940874608\",\"ga_tracking_id\":null,\"tiktok_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_checkout_initiated_pixel_id\":null,\"twitter_purchase_pixel_id\":null,\"google_ads_conversion_id\":null,\"google_ads_purchase_convers