\"Gigs\"}],\"impression_id\":\"8fa9a59af65bb1b7:38\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"16812\",\"name\":\"The Alban Arena\",\"address\":\"Civic Centre, St Albans, AL1 3LD, Hertfordshire, England, United Kingdom\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.752891,\"lng\":-0.336431},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"6419837b1eefa2175ae0f852\",\"name\":\"St Albans\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.751736,\"lng\":-0.339166,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"the-alban-arena-q2koa\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":null},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-06-13T18:30:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Bruce Foxton\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"126856\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":1,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"about\":{\"description\":\"BRUCE FOXTON\\n\\n& his all-star band\\n\\n\\\\+ support: TBC\\n\\nBruce Foxton of The Jam and Stiff Little Fingers announces 2026 UK tour dates with his new all-star band.\\n\\nThe career of Bruce Foxton spans almost 5 decades. He came to prominence as bassist/vocalist and songwriter for The Jam, writing and performing the lead vocals on 'News of the World', 'Smithers-Jones' along with The Kinks cover 'David Watts'.\\n\\nAfter the break of The Jam, Bruce Foxton released a solo album, 'Touch Sensitive', in 1984. He joined Stiff Little Fingers and toured and recorded with the band for over 15 years.\\n\\nFollowing his departure from Stiff Little Fingers, Bruce Foxton joined up with ex-The Jam drummer Rick Buckler, and guitarist/vocalist Russell Hastings in 2007 to tour as From The Jam.\\n\\nAn AGMP Concerts presentation.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 16+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"seating\":null,\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2025-11-27T14:27:22+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-06-13T09:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2025-11-27T14:27:22+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-06-13T18:30:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-06-13T22:30:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"properties\":[],\"id\":\"69287a888aacf60001fabcb7\",\"name\":\"Bruce Foxton\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-27/14f65ef3-b727-41c4-bbba-c278ce1fda0e.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C1080%2C1080\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-27/14f65ef3-b727-41c4-bbba-c278ce1fda0e.jpg?rect=0%2C216%2C1080%2C648\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-11-27/14f65ef3-b727-41c4-bbba-c278ce1fda0e.jpg?rect=243%2C0%2C594%2C1080\"},\"marketeers\":[],\"new\":false,\"offers_extras\":false,\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"announcement_date_unix\":1764253642,\"donation\":null,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":false,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r5f6bbae6084?dice_id=r5f6bbae6084\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/uccbe9e82a96?dice_id=uccbe9e82a96\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/W5058c2b91a1?dice_id=W5058c2b91a1\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/K87ea9f11527?dice_id=K87ea9f11527\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Ge103b84d7a5?dice_id=Ge103b84d7a5\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/La15882dae6f?dice_id=La15882dae6f\"},\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"previews\":[],\"score\":0,\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"event_tag\":null},{\"unicorn\":true,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":3300,\"sales_tax\":0,\"amount_from\":null},\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by DMP.\",\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"faqs\":[],\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"1768\",\"name\":\"DMP\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"dmp-d5kq\",\"profile_active\":false},\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"perm_name\":\"av3rnx-jesse-malin-13th-jun-union-chapel-london-tickets\",\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"secondary_status\":null,\"date_unix\":1781373600,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"max_tickets\":6,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"impression_id\":\"8fa9a59af65bb1b7:39\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"65\",\"name\":\"Union Chapel\",\"address\":\"Compton Terrace, London N1 2UN, UK\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.5447669,\"lng\":-0.102892500000053},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"accuracy\":12,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"54d8a87238fe5d27d500988a\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"union-chapel-jx9a\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.unionchapel.org.uk/accessibility\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-06-13T18:30:00+01:00\",\"doors_close_date\":null}],\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[{\"name\":\"Jesse Malin\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-02-27/e4f86724-bce0-40c6-a98a-db28ae7fbbde.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C640%2C640\"},\"artist_id\":\"722\",\"about\":{\"description\":\"Hailed by Rolling Stone as “a gritty troubadour of the streets,” Jesse Malin released his solo debut, The Fine Art Of Self Destruction, to universal acclaim in 2003, with Uncut dubbing the album “an instant classic” and The Times declaring that “there is simply nothing more you can demand from a great rock record.” Over the next two decades, Malin would go on to release eight more similarly lauded solo albums while building a loyal community of diehard fans across the UK and Europe, spreading the gospel of New York rock and roll and PMA (Positive Mental Attitude) through sold-out headline tours and festival performances everywhere from Glastonbury to Hyde Park. A true songwriter’s songwriter, Malin has recorded with and covered by Bruce Springsteen and Lucinda Williams, shared stages with The Replacements, The Gaslight Anthem, Green Day, and Bob Weir, and seen his songs covered by the likes of Elvis Costello, Bleachers, Counting Crows, Green Day, The Wallflowers, Ian Hunter, Frank Turner, Dinosaur Jr., and more.\\n\\nIn 2023, Malin suffered a rare spinal stroke, which left him paralyzed from the waist down. Rather than retreat from the spotlight, he defied the odds and learned to stand again, returning to the stage the following year in America with two triumphant sold-out nights at NYC’s legendary Beacon Theatre before crossing the pond for a pair of sold-out shows at London’s Islington Assembly Hall.\\n\\nIn 2026, Jesse is making his off-Broadway debut in the acclaimed stage show Silver Manhattan, written by Malin and Lauren Ludwig, and produced by ArKtype and David Bason. His first book Almost Grown: A New York Memoir will be released April 7 (Akashic)\\n\\nMalin will return to the UK in June for a limited three-night engagement in Glasgow, Manchester, and London starting June 11 to June 13 in London at the Union Chapel.\",\"highlights\":[]},\"is_headliner\":true},{\"name\":\"Diane Gentile\",\"image\":null,\"artist_id\":\"58213\",\"about\":null,\"is_headliner\":false}],\"total_artists\":2,\"total_free_texts\":0},\"about\":{\"description\":\"Hailed by Rolling Stone as “a gritty troubadour of the streets,” Jesse Malin released his solo debut, The Fine Art Of Self Destruction, to universal acclaim in 2003, with Uncut dubbing the album “an instant classic” and The Times declaring that “there is simply nothing more you can demand from a great rock record.” Over the next two decades, Malin would go on to release eight more similarly lauded solo albums while building a loyal community of diehard fans across the UK and Europe, spreading the gospel of New York rock and roll and PMA (Positive Mental Attitude) through sold-out headline tours and festival performances everywhere from Glastonbury to Hyde Park. A true songwriter’s songwriter, Malin has recorded with and covered by Bruce Springsteen and Lucinda Williams, shared stages with The Replacements, The Gaslight Anthem, Green Day, and Bob Weir, and seen his songs covered by the likes of Elvis Costello, Bleachers, Counting Crows, Green Day, The Wallflowers, Ian Hunter, Frank Turner, Dinosaur Jr., and more.\\n\\nIn 2023, Malin suffered a rare spinal stroke, which left him paralyzed from the waist down. Rather than retreat from the spotlight, he defied the odds and learned to stand again, returning to the stage the following year in America with two triumphant sold-out nights at NYC’s legendary Beacon Theatre before crossing the pond for a pair of sold-out shows at London’s Islington Assembly Hall.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"All ages - Under 16s to be accompanied by an adult\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"seating\":null,\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2026-01-27T12:00:00+00:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-06-13T18:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2026-01-27T12:00:00+00:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-06-13T19:00:00+01:00\",\"event_end_date\":\"2026-06-13T22:30:00+01:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false,\"pre_sale_start_date\":null},\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"properties\":[],\"id\":\"697803eacc43c90001dff6c3\",\"name\":\"Jesse Malin\",\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-27/687c1a58-83bc-48f8-95bf-7f97501b33bc.jpg?rect=503%2C0%2C2019%2C2019\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-27/687c1a58-83bc-48f8-95bf-7f97501b33bc.jpg?rect=0%2C103%2C3024%2C1814\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-27/687c1a58-83bc-48f8-95bf-7f97501b33bc.jpg?rect=957%