d=w1d92835b257\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/rbe9f4a298f6?dice_id=rbe9f4a298f6\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Qc5e2744bef1?dice_id=Qc5e2744bef1\"},\"perm_name\":\"3on6vx-dear-boy-and-the-noise-portrait-generation-peach-rebels-3rd-jul-hot-box-chelmsford-tickets\",\"secondary_status\":null,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-10/61b6c5a1-c441-4a02-b6bf-b2f517449eb9.jpg?rect=0%2C149%2C1687%2C1687\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-10/61b6c5a1-c441-4a02-b6bf-b2f517449eb9.jpg?rect=0%2C487%2C1687%2C1012\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2025-12-10/61b6c5a1-c441-4a02-b6bf-b2f517449eb9.jpg?rect=298%2C0%2C1092%2C1985\"},\"properties\":[],\"about\":{\"description\":\"Hailing from the heart of Chelmsford, Essex, ***Dear Boy and The Noise*** are an unapologetically loud, high-voltage rock and roll force built on blistering energy and raw musical grit. Their sound hits fast and hard—energetic, fast-paced anthems driven by loud, overdriven guitars, thundering drums, and heavy, chest-rattling basslines that refuse to sit quietly in the background.\\n\\nFormed by four friends with a shared love for chaos, melody, and making the walls shake, the band features:\\n\\nRichard Tuckey – Lead guitar\\n\\nKody Edwards – Vocals\\n\\nMax Campbell – bass\\n\\nNoah Booth – drums\\n\\nTogether, they carve out a sonic identity that’s both modern and soaked in classic rock swagger—melding fierce riffs, punchy rhythms, and hook-laden choruses into a live show that’s as intense as it is unforgettable.\\n\\nWhether they’re tearing up small clubs or shaking festival stages, Dear Boy and The Noise deliver one promise every time: it’s going to be loud, it’s going to be fast, and you’re going to feel it.\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"id\":\"6939c1b5a570f2000156c8c0\",\"