se,\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/eb747b46-db52-49d9-a0cd-fab642e9524c.jpg?rect=0%2C0%2C1080%2C1080\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/eb747b46-db52-49d9-a0cd-fab642e9524c.jpg?rect=0%2C216%2C1080%2C648\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-01-16/eb747b46-db52-49d9-a0cd-fab642e9524c.jpg?rect=243%2C0%2C594%2C1080\"},\"previews\":[{\"type\":\"apple_music\",\"title\":\"Zoe Schwarz Blue Commotion - The Blues and I Should Have a Party (feat. Rob Koral, Pete Whittaker & Paul Robinson)\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://music.apple.com/us/album/the-blues-and-i-should-have-a-party-feat-rob/1617418807?i=1617418809&uo=4&at=1001ld8Z&ct=app_event\",\"artist\":\"Zoe Schwarz Blue Commotion\",\"preview_url\":\"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview122/v4/5c/95/f9/5c95f9a3-c0fb-0d16-0f8a-26399f0422d9/mzaf_11146683365761114179.plus.aac.p.m4a\",\"track_name\":\"The Blues and I Should Have a Party (feat. Rob Koral, Pete Whittaker & Paul Robinson)\"},{\"type\":\"spotify\",\"title\":\"Zoe Schwarz Blue Commotion - The Blues and I Should Have a Party\",\"redirect_url\":\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2EnXxnVQFP3urol9G4GnFp\",\"artist\":\"Zoe Schwarz Blue Commotion\",\"preview_url\":\"https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/cb4dc5ec54f6ed10cf4ff6b1e0115720d3ada20c?cid=921526b9c2da4b7b96e197790a02347e\",\"track_name\":\"The Blues and I Should Have a Party\"}],\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"announcement_date_unix\":1768521600,\"max_tickets\":6,\"marketeers\":[],\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"gig\",\"value\":\"music:gig\",\"title\":\"Gigs\"}],\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"seating\":null,\"about\":{\"description\":\"\\\"Eye catching vocals meet sumptuous guitar”- Guitarist Magazine\\n\\n\\\"Terrific musicians. Very nice indeed” - Paul Jones Rhythm & Blues, BBC radio 2\\n\\n\\\"Recommended” - Jamie Cullum, BBC radio 2\\n\\n\\\"A perfect mix of head and heart’ - Ronnie Scott’s Magazine\\n\\nThe first Blue Commotion gig in February 2012 was a culmination of a ten-year musical partnership between Zoë Schwarz and guitarist Rob Koral. Through their intense musical journey and compatible desire, they developed a perfect collaboration and empathy, which, when analysed, comes from two completely different starting points. Because of this melting pot of musical diversity, there is a depth and uniqueness to the band's music, which is hard to pigeonhole and categorise.\\n\\nInto the mix comes the sheer virtuosity of each of the band members who are allowed the freedom to express their musical authority, and stamp their own personal magic to the song writing of Zoë and Rob. A testament to this chemistry is the sheer volume of music coming out of the band, and CHAMELEON was the band’s seventh album in eight years as at April 2020.\\n\\nZoe and Rob are a “nationally regarded couple, it tells in the power and professionalism of their performance…”. Their regular Rhythm section is; Pete Whittaker-Hammond organ (Wonderstuff, John Ethridge, Nigel Price, Theo Travis, Filthy Six and more), and Eddie John-drums (Pee Wee Ellis, Jim Mullen, Stackridge, Digby Fairweather, Tina May and more).\",\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an 18+ event\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"shopping_cart_enabled\":false,\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Hot Box Live Community Interest\",\"streaming_options\":null,\"impression_id\":\"e551cd9f216396a3:89\",\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/H8fad6bcdabf?dice_id=H8fad6bcdabf\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/E408a59f0934?dice_id=E408a59f0934\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/pc52d22847c3?dice_id=pc52d22847c3\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/U57c1f0a9d28?dice_id=U57c1f0a9d28\",\"post_reminde